{"title":"Constant function","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>constant function</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> which has a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constant</a> output: the value of the function does not depend on the value of its input.  Equivalently, a constant function is a function whose <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Range\" title=\"Range\">range</a> has only a single value. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33b44150f1e721cf75910c2220cf159d371a7694.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> is a constant function because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> always equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb4d86f587cf7c0447409d36895f830a6981a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=\\log_{34} e^{\\pi-\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"22\" /> is a constant function since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c575f9c97ea1e06ffcde3240c9733ec732ac5b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{34} e^{\\pi-\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"22\" /> is always equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c575f9c97ea1e06ffcde3240c9733ec732ac5b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{34} e^{\\pi-\\frac{1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"22\" />. So, basically, a constant function is a function that for whatever input you put in, it always returns the same value, or a constant. These functions are not included with the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_Root_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rational Root Theorem\">Rational Root Theorem</a> since they usually do not have roots (unless the constant function is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/c/a8c9cbf3e3c04dc46dea71f60acd0cb704eabc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />)\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Constant_function&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018081445\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 28/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1297/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.982      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.982      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4516:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018081445 and revision id 219155. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}